;*********************************************************************;;                 Implementation of an 'IDataObject';;     This file should be saved under the name "IDataObject.pbi".;;                  For Windows only - PB 6.11 -> 6.4;                       November 2026 - Zapman;;*********************************************************************;; Big thanks to Nico from the PureBasic Forum. As far as I know,; he was the first to try to implement an IDataObject in PureBasic,; and he did a significant part of the work presented here.;; Ten years ago, starting from his work, I began developing this; project to add Drag'n Drop functionality to one of my programs.; During 2024, I finally decided to push the implementation as far; as I could, in order to obtain a fully functional IDataObject; for any future purpose.;; This implementation allows the IDataObject to support the 'SetData',; 'GetData', and 'GetDataHere' methods for most possible formats, as well; as on-demand delayed rendering via 'RegisterDelayedData()'.; The object also responds to requests for EnumFormatEtc, EnumDAdvise,; QueryGetData, GetCanonicalFormatEtc, QueryInterface, AddRef,; DAdvise, DUnadvise, and Release.;; This IDataObject is designed to be as generic as possible, but,; of course, you can adapt its code to your specific needs.;;; The 'IDataObject' interface in Windows allows manipulating and transferring data; between different applications or processes, for example, via the clipboard or; drag-and-drop. It provides access to data in multiple formats, grouped in an object; that other applications can use. The main methods are GetData (to retrieve data),; SetData (to set data), and EnumFormatEtc (to list available data formats). IDataObject; is often used in OLE environments to link or embed objects in documents or applications.;; In Windows, an object represents an entity that contains data and functions.; An object has interfaces, which are ways to access its features, such as; reading files or managing data streams. Objects in Windows often use; COM (Component Object Model), where a base interface like IUnknown manages; references and communication between objects. This model helps software components; work well together by adhering to specific interface rules.;; Object-oriented programming (OOP) organizes code into objects that contain both; data (called properties) and functions (called methods) to manipulate them.; Each object is like a small autonomous unit, representing something from the real; world, like a window or a file. This makes programs more structured and reusable.; Objects can interact with each other, making the code more flexible and modular.;; In comparison, traditional programming, often called 'procedural programming',; follows a linear plan where instructions are executed one after another. Data; and functions are separated, and the program is usually organized into large; sequences of code. Although simpler at first, this approach can show limitations; when managing large projects with many interactions between different parts of; the program. These limitations can be perfectly handled with a solid structure; and by segmenting the code into more or less autonomous procedures. However, some prefer; a more radical approach where each feature is organized as an independent object; with a strict list of "methods" that allow interacting with it. This is the choice; made for many subsets of Windows functions, and it is now inevitable, when; interacting with Windows through its APIs, to understand the principles of this; programming paradigm.;; For everything related to data manipulation (reading and writing files,; copy-pasting, audio and video streams, drag and drop, and screen display),; it is almost essential, if you want to overcome certain limitations of PureBasic's; built-in functions, to know how to create and manage an IDataObject. Unfortunately,; while Windows often imposes the use of this type of Object, no API provides; a simple way to create it, and a quick look at forums for various programming; languages shows that this question comes up very often: "How do you create an IDataObject?";; This library was designed to answer that question.;; As mentioned earlier, an 'Object' contains both data and 'Methods'; allowing interaction with this data.; What must be strictly respected for our IDataObject to function properly; is the number of its methods, the roles they must play, the number and type of; parameters they must accept as input, and the values they must provide as output.;; However, the way the data is stored internally is almost entirely free, even though; the data itself must be formatted according to criteria set by Windows.;;             ********************************************************;;-                                   The Data;;             ********************************************************;; The data of an IDataObject is always defined by two structures that work; in tandem:; • A FORMATETC structure that indicates what kind of data it is.;     - FORMATETC tells us, for example, if it is ASCII text (CF_TEXT), Unicode text;       (CF_UNICODETEXT), a bitmap image (CF_BITMAP), a DIB-encoded bitmap (CF_DIB),;       an image encoded in a metafile (CF_METAFILEPICT), etc.;     - Through its 'tymed' field, FORMATETC also informs us how the data is stored:;       on disk, in memory, in a stream, etc.; • A STGMEDIUM structure that contains the data or specifies how to access it.;       Simple data usually consists of memory blocks referenced directly in STGMEDIUM.;       Heavier data is often stored in external sources to which STGMEDIUM provides;       access. And since Windows loves "Objects", it is not uncommon for STGMEDIUM;       to simply provide the interface of another object that must be queried to;       retrieve the data.;; Prototype for optional delayed-rendering callbacks registered via RegisterDelayedData():; Must populate *StgMediumOut according to *FormatEtc and return #S_OK on success (or a COM HRESULT error).Prototype.i ProtoIDORenderData(*pDataObject.IDataObject, *FormatEtc.FORMATETC, *StgMediumOut.STGMEDIUM, UserData);; Each FORMATETC-STGMEDIUM pair belonging to an IDataObject is stored in an 'IDO_EntryStruct':;Structure IDO_EntryStruct  ; Combines a FORMATETC descriptor with its corresponding STGMEDIUM storage  ; (or a delayed-rendering callback until the data is requested for the first time).  m_stgmed.StgMedium ; Stores the STGMEDIUM structure  m_format.FormatEtc ; Stores the FORMATETC structure  *RenderCallback    ; Optional ProtoIDORenderData callback for delayed rendering (#Null once rendered)  UserData.i         ; Optional user value passed to *RenderCallbackEndStructure;; Next, we define 'IDO_DetailsStruct', which gathers the address of the IDataObject; VTable, its dynamic list of data entries, its reference count, and its advise holder:;Structure IDO_DetailsStruct  ; Gathers everything necessary for the operation of an independent IDataObject instance.  pDataObject.IDataObject             ; Pointer to the IDataObject VTable (MUST remain at offset 0)  Refcount.l                          ; Reference count tracking active users of this object  List Entries.IDO_EntryStruct()      ; Unlimited list of FORMATETC/STGMEDIUM entries owned by this object  pDataAdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder ; Standard OLE advise holder used for DAdvise managementEndStructure;NewList IDO_Details.IDO_DetailsStruct()Global IDO_Mutex = CreateMutex();; The IDO_Details.IDO_DetailsStruct() list keeps our active objects in memory; as long as necessary, protected by IDO_Mutex for thread-safe access when Windows; Shell or OLE worker threads query the object concurrently.; Each element of IDO_Details() represents an independent IDataObject with its own Entries() list.;; A pointer to one of our IDataObjects also points to the IDO_DetailsStruct; associated with it and to the element of the IDO_Details() list that contains this IDO_DetailsStruct.; All of these reside at the exact same memory address.; This may seem strange to developers unfamiliar with pointers, but you can write:;   CurrentRefCount = *UPointer\Refcount ; (with *UPointer.IDO_DetailsStruct);   *MyData.IDataObject = *UPointer;   ChangeCurrentElement(IDO_Details(), *UPointer); using the exact same value for *UPointer.;; This is because a pointer to a PureBasic list element points directly to; the data content of that element, and a pointer to a structure points to; its first field (offset 0).; Because our IDO_DetailsStruct structure has pDataObject as its first field, a pointer to; this structure points directly to pDataObject.;; Nothing else is needed to store the data.;;     ********************************************************;;-                        The 'Methods';;     ********************************************************;; What is called a 'method' in object-oriented programming (OOP); is simply a procedure in PureBasic. And a COM 'object' is essentially; a pointer to a table of 'methods' capable of manipulating the object's data.; This collection of 'methods' is called an interface (VTable).;; When a process calls an object through the 'QueryInterface' method,; it asks the object to return a pointer to this table of method addresses.;; This list appears at the end of this file in the DataSection:;; DataSection;   VTable_IDataObject:;     Data.i @dataobject_QueryInterface(), @dataobject_AddRef(), @dataobject_Release();     Data.i @dataobject_GetData(), @dataobject_GetDataHere(), @dataobject_QueryGetData();     Data.i @dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc(), @dataobject_SetData(), @dataobject_EnumFormatEtc();     Data.i @dataobject_DAdvise(), @dataobject_DUnAdvise(), @dataobject_EnumDAdvise(); EndDataSection;; An IDataObject must expose twelve methods arranged in the exact order shown above,; strictly adhering to Microsoft's IDataObject specification.;; Before tackling those twelve methods, let's look at the procedures YOU will call; to create an IDataObject, register delayed data if needed, verify it, and destroy it:;;      ********************************************************;;-           Creation and Destruction of the IDataObject;;      ********************************************************;Procedure CreateIDataObject()  ;  ; Role: Creates a new IDataObject instance in memory with an initial COM reference count of 1.  ; Output: Returns a pointer to the newly created IDataObject (and its underlying IDO_DetailsStruct).  ;  Shared IDO_Details()  Protected *Result  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  If AddElement(IDO_Details())    IDO_Details()\pDataObject = ?VTable_IDataObject    IDO_Details()\Refcount = 1    *Result = IDO_Details()  EndIf  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  ProcedureReturn *ResultEndProcedure;Procedure IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet)  ;  ; Role: Checks in a thread-safe manner whether the given pointer corresponds to an active IDataObject.  ; Output: Returns #True if the object exists in IDO_Details(), #False otherwise.  ;  Shared IDO_Details()  Protected Found = #False  ;  If *DataObjectDet    LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    ForEach IDO_Details()      If IDO_Details() = *DataObjectDet        Found = #True        Break      EndIf    Next    UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn FoundEndProcedure;Procedure DestroyIDataObject(*pDataObject.IDataObject)  ;  ; Role: Unconditionally releases all references to *pDataObject, frees all owned data,  ;       detaches it from the clipboard if it is the current clipboard owner, and removes it from memory.  ;  If IsIDataObject(*pDataObject)    ; Ensure Windows does not keep a dangling pointer if this object is currently on the clipboard    ; (Called outside any mutex lock to prevent cross-thread OLE deadlocks)    If OleIsCurrentClipboard_(*pDataObject) = #S_OK      OleSetClipboard_(#Null)    EndIf    ; Force release of all remaining references until the object destroys itself (Release returns 0)    While IsIDataObject(*pDataObject) And *pDataObject\Release() > 0 : Wend  Else    Debug "Wrong parameter for DestroyIDataObject(): this object does not exist."  EndIfEndProcedure;; Note: CreateIDataObject() initializes Refcount to 1 (representing the creator's reference).; If you hand over the object to Windows (for instance via OleSetClipboard_ + OleFlushClipboard_,; or DoDragDrop_) and want COM to destroy it naturally once no external process uses it anymore,; call *pDataObject\Release() once. Call DestroyIDataObject() when you want immediate forced cleanup.;; ********************************************************;;-                 Debugging Procedure;; ********************************************************;; Set SilentMethods = 0 to log every COM interaction in the PureBasic Debug window.;Global SilentMethods = 1;Procedure IDO_RegisterResults(Mess$)  ;  ; Role: Outputs trace messages to the debugger when SilentMethods is disabled (0).  ;  If SilentMethods = 0    Debug Mess$  EndIfEndProcedure;; ********************************************************;;-                 Generic Procedures;; ********************************************************;CompilerIf Not Defined(GetWinErrorMessage, #PB_Procedure)  Procedure.s GetWinErrorMessage(errorCode = 0)    ;    ; Role: Translates a Windows API or COM HRESULT error code into a descriptive message string.    ; Parameters: errorCode - Error code to translate (if 0, calls GetLastError_() automatically).    ; Output: Returns the formatted error description followed by its hexadecimal code.    ;    Protected messageBuffer$    Protected MLength, length, ErrorN, MHandle    ;    If errorCode = 0      errorCode = GetLastError_()    EndIf    If errorCode      MLength = 500      messageBuffer$ = Space((MLength + 1) * 2)      length = FormatMessage_(#FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_SYSTEM, #Null, errorCode, 0, @messageBuffer$, MLength, #Null)      If length < 1        #ERROR_INTERNET_EXTENDED_ERROR = 12003        If errorCode = #ERROR_INTERNET_EXTENDED_ERROR          ErrorN = 0          length = InternetGetLastResponseInfo_(@ErrorN, @messageBuffer$, @MLength)          If length = 0            length = FormatMessage_(#FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_SYSTEM, #Null, GetLastError_(), 0, @messageBuffer$, MLength, #Null)          EndIf        ElseIf errorCode > 11999 And errorCode < 13000          #FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_HMODULE = $00000800          MHandle = GetModuleHandle_("wininet.dll")          length = FormatMessage_(#FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_HMODULE, MHandle, errorCode, 0, @messageBuffer$, MLength, #Null)        EndIf      EndIf      messageBuffer$ = ReplaceString(messageBuffer$, #LF$, "")      messageBuffer$ = ReplaceString(messageBuffer$, #CR$, "")      messageBuffer$ = Trim(messageBuffer$)      If messageBuffer$ = ""        messageBuffer$ = "Unknown error"      EndIf      ProcedureReturn messageBuffer$ + "  ($" + Hex(errorCode, #PB_Long) + ")"    EndIf    ;    ProcedureReturn ""  EndProcedureCompilerEndIf;Procedure.s GetFormatName(cfFormat.w)  ;  ; Role: Resolves a clipboard format identifier (standard or registered) into its readable name.  ; Output: Returns the standard CF_* constant name, the registered clipboard format name, or "Unknown format".  ;  Protected formatName$, NameLen  Protected Format = cfFormat & $FFFF ; Convert signed 16-bit word to unsigned 16-bit integer (0..65535)  ;  Select Format    ; Standard Windows clipboard formats    Case #CF_TEXT            : formatName$ = "CF_TEXT"    Case #CF_BITMAP          : formatName$ = "CF_BITMAP"    Case #CF_METAFILEPICT    : formatName$ = "CF_METAFILEPICT"    Case #CF_SYLK            : formatName$ = "CF_SYLK"    Case #CF_DIF             : formatName$ = "CF_DIF"    Case #CF_TIFF            : formatName$ = "CF_TIFF"    Case #CF_OEMTEXT         : formatName$ = "CF_OEMTEXT"    Case #CF_DIB             : formatName$ = "CF_DIB"    Case #CF_PALETTE         : formatName$ = "CF_PALETTE"    Case #CF_PENDATA         : formatName$ = "CF_PENDATA"    Case #CF_RIFF            : formatName$ = "CF_RIFF"    Case #CF_WAVE            : formatName$ = "CF_WAVE"    Case #CF_UNICODETEXT     : formatName$ = "CF_UNICODETEXT"    Case #CF_ENHMETAFILE     : formatName$ = "CF_ENHMETAFILE"    Case #CF_HDROP           : formatName$ = "CF_HDROP"    Case #CF_LOCALE          : formatName$ = "CF_LOCALE"    Case #CF_DIBV5           : formatName$ = "CF_DIBV5"    ; Special display and range clipboard formats    Case #CF_OWNERDISPLAY    : formatName$ = "CF_OWNERDISPLAY"    Case #CF_DSPTEXT         : formatName$ = "CF_DSPTEXT"    Case #CF_DSPBITMAP       : formatName$ = "CF_DSPBITMAP"    Case #CF_DSPMETAFILEPICT : formatName$ = "CF_DSPMETAFILEPICT"    Case #CF_DSPENHMETAFILE  : formatName$ = "CF_DSPENHMETAFILE"    Case #CF_PRIVATEFIRST    : formatName$ = "CF_PRIVATEFIRST"    Case #CF_PRIVATELAST     : formatName$ = "CF_PRIVATELAST"    Case #CF_GDIOBJFIRST     : formatName$ = "CF_GDIOBJFIRST"    Case #CF_GDIOBJLAST      : formatName$ = "CF_GDIOBJLAST"    Default      ; Query Windows for custom registered clipboard format names (e.g., "Rich Text Format", "PNG")      formatName$ = Space(256)      NameLen = GetClipboardFormatName_(Format, @formatName$, 256)      If NameLen > 0        formatName$ = Left(formatName$, NameLen)      Else        formatName$ = "Unknown format (" + Str(Format) + ")"      EndIf  EndSelect  ;  ProcedureReturn formatName$EndProcedure;Procedure.s GetTymedName(Tymed)  ;  ; Role: Converts a TYMED bitmask value into a readable combination of TYMED_* constant names.  ;  Protected Tymed$  ;  If Tymed = #TYMED_NULL    Tymed$ = "TYMED_NULL"  Else    ; Decode each bit flag present in the Tymed bitmask    If Tymed & #TYMED_HGLOBAL  : Tymed$ + "TYMED_HGLOBAL + "  : EndIf    If Tymed & #TYMED_FILE     : Tymed$ + "TYMED_FILE + "     : EndIf    If Tymed & #TYMED_ISTREAM  : Tymed$ + "TYMED_ISTREAM + "  : EndIf    If Tymed & #TYMED_ISTORAGE : Tymed$ + "TYMED_ISTORAGE + " : EndIf    If Tymed & #TYMED_GDI      : Tymed$ + "TYMED_GDI + "      : EndIf    If Tymed & #TYMED_MFPICT   : Tymed$ + "TYMED_MFPICT + "   : EndIf    If Tymed & #TYMED_ENHMF    : Tymed$ + "TYMED_ENHMF + "    : EndIf    ;    If Tymed$ = ""      Tymed$ = "Unknown tymed value: " + Str(Tymed)    Else      ; Strip the trailing " + " separator      Tymed$ = Left(Tymed$, Len(Tymed$) - 3)    EndIf  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn Tymed$EndProcedure;Procedure.s StringFromCLSID(*MyCLSID)  ;  ; Role: Converts a 16-byte binary GUID/CLSID/IID in memory into its canonical string representation.  ; Parameters: *MyCLSID - Memory address of the 16-byte GUID structure.  ;  Protected *CLSIDString, Ret$  ;  If *MyCLSID = #Null    ProcedureReturn "NULL CLSID"  EndIf  ;  If StringFromCLSID_(*MyCLSID, @*CLSIDString) = #S_OK And *CLSIDString    Ret$ = PeekS(*CLSIDString, -1, #PB_Unicode)    CoTaskMemFree_(*CLSIDString)  Else    Ret$ = "Error while converting CLSID to String."  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn Ret$EndProcedure;Procedure CloneIDataObject(*IDOSource.IDataObject, *IDODest.IDataObject)  ;  ; Role: Copies all available #DATADIR_GET data formats and media from *IDOSource into *IDODest.  ;  Protected *enumFormat.IEnumFORMATETC, SC  Protected formatEtc.FormatEtc, stgm.StgMedium  ;  If *IDOSource = #Null Or *IDODest = #Null    Debug "CloneIDataObject error: Source or destination IDataObject is null."    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  SC = *IDOSource\EnumFormatEtc(#DATADIR_GET, @*enumFormat)  If SC = #S_OK And *enumFormat    ; Iterate through all available formats exposed by the source object    While *enumFormat\Next(1, @formatEtc, #Null) = #S_OK      SC = *IDOSource\GetData(formatEtc, @stgm)      If SC = #S_OK        SC = *IDODest\SetData(formatEtc, @stgm, #True)        If SC <> #S_OK          ; Per COM rules, if SetData fails, it does not take ownership of stgm; release it here          ReleaseStgMedium_(@stgm)          Debug "CloneIDataObject - Error while setting data (" + GetFormatName(formatEtc\cfFormat) + "): " + GetWinErrorMessage(SC)        EndIf      Else        Debug "CloneIDataObject - Error while getting data (" + GetFormatName(formatEtc\cfFormat) + "): " + GetWinErrorMessage(SC)      EndIf      ; Free any target device structure allocated by EnumFormatEtc\Next      If formatEtc\ptd        CoTaskMemFree_(formatEtc\ptd)        formatEtc\ptd = #Null      EndIf    Wend    ; Release the enumerator    *enumFormat\Release()  Else    Debug "CloneIDataObject - Error: Unable to open format enumerator."  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn SCEndProcedure;; *******************************************************************;;-     Auxiliary procedures, essential for the operation;                          of the IDataObject;; *******************************************************************;Procedure.i IsPTRValid(*ptr)  ;  ; Role: Verifies that a memory address points to committed, readable virtual memory.  ; Output: Returns #True if the pointer is safe to read, #False otherwise.  ;  Protected mbi.MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION  ;  If *ptr    If VirtualQuery_(*ptr, @mbi, SizeOf(MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION))      If mbi\State = #MEM_COMMIT And (mbi\Protect & (#PAGE_NOACCESS | #PAGE_GUARD)) = 0        ProcedureReturn #True      EndIf    EndIf  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn #FalseEndProcedure;Procedure CloneStgMedium(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *StgMed_Source.STGMedium, *StgMed_Dest.STGMedium, *AskedFormatEtc.FormatEtc, Method$ = "")  ;  ; Role: Duplicates the storage medium from *StgMed_Source into *StgMed_Dest according to the COM call context.  ;       Supports TYMED_GDI (#CF_BITMAP and #CF_PALETTE), TYMED_HGLOBAL, TYMED_ENHMF, TYMED_MFPICT,  ;       TYMED_FILE, TYMED_ISTORAGE, TYMED_ISTREAM, and TYMED_NULL, as well as bidirectional on-the-fly  ;       conversion between HGLOBAL/MFPICT and ISTREAM.  ; Parameters:  ;   *DataObjectDet  - Pointer to the owning IDO_DetailsStruct.  ;   *StgMed_Source  - Source STGMEDIUM containing the data to duplicate.  ;   *StgMed_Dest    - Destination STGMEDIUM to populate (or pre-allocated by caller when Method$ = "GetDataHere").  ;   *AskedFormatEtc - Requested FORMATETC specifying cfFormat and acceptable tymed bitmask.  ;   Method$         - Call context: "GetData", "GetDataHere", "SetData", or "".  ; Output: Returns #S_OK on success, or a standard COM HRESULT error code.  ;  Protected RetValue, GenerateIStream, GenerateHGlobal, InvalidSourceErr, PathByteLen  Protected *StreamSrc.IStream, *StreamRead.IStream, IStreamTest.IStream, IStorageTest.IStorage  Protected TempHGlobal, *GlobalPtr, BytesRead.l  Protected bytesToCopy.q, SavedPos.q, LogPrefix$  ;  ; Validate input parameters  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    MessageRequester("Oops!", "Program error: Non-existent *DataObjectDet while calling CloneStgMedium.")    ProcedureReturn #E_FAIL  ElseIf *StgMed_Source = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("CloneStgMedium  --> Error with DataSource: *** NULL ARGUMENT ***")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  ElseIf *StgMed_Dest = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("CloneStgMedium  --> Error with DataDest: *** NULL ARGUMENT ***")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  ElseIf *AskedFormatEtc = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("CloneStgMedium  --> Error with *AskedFormatEtc: *** NULL ARGUMENT ***")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  ElseIf Method$ <> "" And Method$ <> "GetData" And Method$ <> "SetData" And Method$ <> "GetDataHere"    IDO_RegisterResults("CloneStgMedium  --> Error with Method$: *** ''" + Method$ + "'' VALUE IS NOT VALID ***")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  If Method$ = "SetData" Or Method$ = ""    InvalidSourceErr = #E_INVALIDARG  Else    InvalidSourceErr = #E_UNEXPECTED  EndIf  ;  ; Check if on-the-fly medium conversion (HGLOBAL/MFPICT -> ISTREAM or ISTREAM -> HGLOBAL) is requested  If Method$ <> "SetData" And (*AskedFormatEtc\tymed & *StgMed_Source\tymed) = 0    If (*AskedFormatEtc\tymed & #TYMED_ISTREAM) And (*StgMed_Source\tymed = #TYMED_HGLOBAL Or *StgMed_Source\tymed = #TYMED_MFPICT)      GenerateIStream = #True    ElseIf (*AskedFormatEtc\tymed & #TYMED_HGLOBAL) And *StgMed_Source\tymed = #TYMED_ISTREAM      GenerateHGlobal = #True    EndIf  EndIf  ;  ; Initialize destination medium when not writing into a caller-allocated GetDataHere medium  If Method$ <> "GetDataHere"    If GenerateIStream      *StgMed_Dest\tymed = #TYMED_ISTREAM    ElseIf GenerateHGlobal      *StgMed_Dest\tymed = #TYMED_HGLOBAL    Else      *StgMed_Dest\tymed = *StgMed_Source\tymed    EndIf    *StgMed_Dest\pUnkForRelease = #Null    *StgMed_Dest\hGlobal        = #Null  EndIf  ;  ; Branch cleanly according to the source storage medium type  Select *StgMed_Source\tymed    Case #TYMED_GDI, #TYMED_HGLOBAL, #TYMED_ENHMF, #TYMED_MFPICT      ; All four handle-based media share the same union slot (hGlobal / hBitmap / hEnhMetaFile / hMetaFilePict)      If *StgMed_Source\tymed = #TYMED_GDI And *AskedFormatEtc\cfFormat <> #CF_BITMAP And *AskedFormatEtc\cfFormat <> #CF_PALETTE        RetValue = #E_NOTIMPL      ElseIf Method$ = "GetDataHere" And GenerateIStream = #False        RetValue = #DV_E_TYMED      ElseIf *StgMed_Source\hGlobal = #Null        If *StgMed_Source\tymed = #TYMED_HGLOBAL And GenerateIStream = #False          ; Allow null HGLOBAL blocks for compatibility with apps like Photoshop that register marker formats          RetValue = #S_OK        Else          RetValue = InvalidSourceErr        EndIf      Else        ; Duplicate the handle using OLE's native duplicator (#GMEM_MOVEABLE ensures clipboard/OLE compatibility)        TempHGlobal = OleDuplicateData_(*StgMed_Source\hGlobal, *AskedFormatEtc\cfFormat, #GMEM_MOVEABLE)        If TempHGlobal = #Null          RetValue = #E_OUTOFMEMORY        ElseIf GenerateIStream = #False          *StgMed_Dest\hGlobal = TempHGlobal          RetValue = #S_OK        Else          ; Synthesize an IStream from TempHGlobal (#True tells COM to free TempHGlobal when the stream is released)          IDO_RegisterResults(" ---> ON-THE-FLY GENERATION OF AN ISTREAM FROM HGLOBAL")          RetValue = CreateStreamOnHGlobal_(TempHGlobal, #True, @*StreamSrc)          If RetValue <> #S_OK Or *StreamSrc = #Null            GlobalFree_(TempHGlobal)            If RetValue = #S_OK : RetValue = #E_OUTOFMEMORY : EndIf          ElseIf Method$ = "GetDataHere"            If *StgMed_Dest\pstm = #Null Or IsPTRValid(*StgMed_Dest\pstm) = #False              RetValue = #E_INVALIDARG            ElseIf *StgMed_Dest\pstm\QueryInterface(?IID_IStream, @IStreamTest) <> #S_OK              RetValue = #E_INVALIDARG            Else              IStreamTest\Release()              *StreamSrc\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_END, @bytesToCopy)              *StreamSrc\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_SET, #Null)              RetValue = *StreamSrc\CopyTo(*StgMed_Dest\pstm, bytesToCopy, #Null, #Null)            EndIf            *StreamSrc\Release()          Else            *StgMed_Dest\pstm = *StreamSrc            *StgMed_Dest\pstm\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_END, #Null)            RetValue = #S_OK          EndIf        EndIf      EndIf      ;    Case #TYMED_ISTORAGE      If *StgMed_Source\pstg = #Null Or IsPTRValid(*StgMed_Source\pstg) = #False        RetValue = InvalidSourceErr      ElseIf Method$ = "GetDataHere"        If *StgMed_Dest\pstg = #Null Or IsPTRValid(*StgMed_Dest\pstg) = #False          RetValue = #E_INVALIDARG        ElseIf *StgMed_Dest\pstg\QueryInterface(?IID_IStorage, @IStorageTest) <> #S_OK          RetValue = #E_INVALIDARG        Else          IStorageTest\Release()          RetValue = *StgMed_Source\pstg\CopyTo(0, #Null, #Null, *StgMed_Dest\pstg)        EndIf      Else        RetValue = *StgMed_Source\pstg\QueryInterface(?IID_IStorage, @*StgMed_Dest\pstg)      EndIf      ;    Case #TYMED_ISTREAM      *StreamSrc = *StgMed_Source\pstm      If *StreamSrc = #Null Or IsPTRValid(*StreamSrc) = #False        RetValue = InvalidSourceErr      ElseIf GenerateHGlobal        ; Synthesize an HGLOBAL block from the source IStream (not applicable to GetDataHere)        If Method$ = "GetDataHere"          RetValue = #DV_E_TYMED        Else          IDO_RegisterResults(" ---> ON-THE-FLY GENERATION OF AN HGLOBAL FROM ISTREAM")          ; Use a cloned stream if possible so we do not alter the source stream's seek pointer          If *StreamSrc\Clone(@*StreamRead) <> #S_OK Or *StreamRead = #Null            *StreamRead = *StreamSrc            *StreamSrc\AddRef()            *StreamRead\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_CUR, @SavedPos)          Else            SavedPos = -1          EndIf          If *StreamRead\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_END, @bytesToCopy) = #S_OK And *StreamRead\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_SET, #Null) = #S_OK            TempHGlobal = GlobalAlloc_(#GMEM_MOVEABLE, bytesToCopy)            If TempHGlobal = #Null              RetValue = #E_OUTOFMEMORY            ElseIf bytesToCopy = 0              *StgMed_Dest\hGlobal = TempHGlobal              RetValue = #S_OK            Else              *GlobalPtr = GlobalLock_(TempHGlobal)              If *GlobalPtr                RetValue = *StreamRead\Read(*GlobalPtr, bytesToCopy, @BytesRead)                GlobalUnlock_(TempHGlobal)                If RetValue = #S_OK Or RetValue = #S_FALSE                  *StgMed_Dest\hGlobal = TempHGlobal                  RetValue = #S_OK                Else                  GlobalFree_(TempHGlobal)                EndIf              Else                GlobalFree_(TempHGlobal)                RetValue = #E_OUTOFMEMORY              EndIf            EndIf          Else            RetValue = #E_FAIL          EndIf          If SavedPos <> -1            *StreamRead\Seek(SavedPos, #STREAM_SEEK_SET, #Null)          EndIf          *StreamRead\Release()        EndIf      ElseIf Method$ = "GetDataHere"        If *StgMed_Dest\pstm = #Null Or IsPTRValid(*StgMed_Dest\pstm) = #False          RetValue = #E_INVALIDARG        ElseIf *StgMed_Dest\pstm\QueryInterface(?IID_IStream, @IStreamTest) <> #S_OK          RetValue = #E_INVALIDARG        Else          IStreamTest\Release()          *StreamSrc\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_END, @bytesToCopy)          *StreamSrc\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_SET, #Null)          RetValue = *StreamSrc\CopyTo(*StgMed_Dest\pstm, bytesToCopy, #Null, #Null)        EndIf      Else        ; Prefer IStream::Clone so source and destination keep independent seek pointers        RetValue = *StreamSrc\Clone(@*StgMed_Dest\pstm)        If RetValue <> #S_OK Or *StgMed_Dest\pstm = #Null          RetValue = *StreamSrc\QueryInterface(?IID_IStream, @*StgMed_Dest\pstm)        EndIf        If RetValue = #S_OK          If Method$ = "SetData"            *StgMed_Dest\pstm\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_SET, #Null)          Else            ; Position seek pointer at the end as required by the Windows OLE inter-process marshaler            *StgMed_Dest\pstm\Seek(0, #STREAM_SEEK_END, #Null)          EndIf        EndIf      EndIf      ;    Case #TYMED_FILE      If Method$ = "GetDataHere"        RetValue = #DV_E_TYMED      ElseIf *StgMed_Source\lpszFileName = #Null        RetValue = InvalidSourceErr      Else        ; Allocate a new OLESTR copy of the file path using CoTaskMemAlloc (required by ReleaseStgMedium for TYMED_FILE)        PathByteLen = (MemoryStringLength(*StgMed_Source\lpszFileName, #PB_Unicode) + 1) * 2        *StgMed_Dest\lpszFileName = CoTaskMemAlloc_(PathByteLen)        If *StgMed_Dest\lpszFileName          CopyMemory(*StgMed_Source\lpszFileName, *StgMed_Dest\lpszFileName, PathByteLen)          RetValue = #S_OK        Else          RetValue = #E_OUTOFMEMORY        EndIf      EndIf      ;    Case #TYMED_NULL      If Method$ = "GetDataHere"        RetValue = #DV_E_TYMED      Else        RetValue = #S_OK      EndIf      ;    Default      RetValue = #E_NOTIMPL  EndSelect  ;  ; Log the outcome of the operation  LogPrefix$ = "dataobject " + Method$ + " for " + GetFormatName(*AskedFormatEtc\cfFormat) + "/" + GetTymedName(*AskedFormatEtc\tymed)  Select RetValue    Case #S_OK      IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " ---> OK")    Case #E_NOTIMPL      IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " *** ERROR *** ---> Format is not supported (" + Str(*AskedFormatEtc\cfFormat & $FFFF) + ").")    Case #E_OUTOFMEMORY      IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " *** ERROR *** ---> Out of memory.")    Case #E_INVALIDARG      IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " *** ERROR *** ---> One or more arguments are invalid.")    Case #E_FAIL      IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " *** ERROR *** ---> Unexpected failure.")    Case #DV_E_TYMED      If Method$ = "GetDataHere"        IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject GetDataHere: " + GetFormatName(*AskedFormatEtc\cfFormat) + "/" + GetTymedName(*AskedFormatEtc\tymed) + " *** ERROR *** ---> Not allowed for GetDataHere.")      Else        IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " *** ERROR *** ---> Tymed type does not match.")      EndIf    Default      IDO_RegisterResults(LogPrefix$ + " *** ERROR *** ---> " + GetWinErrorMessage(RetValue) + ".")  EndSelect  ;  ProcedureReturn RetValueEndProcedure;Procedure IDO_GetDataInternal(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetcIn.FORMATETC, *pmedium.STGMEDIUM, Method$)  ;  ; Role: Shared internal implementation for both 'dataobject_GetData' and 'dataobject_GetDataHere'.  ;       Searches the object's Entries() list for a match with *pformatetcIn, triggers delayed  ;       rendering on first access if needed, and duplicates the medium into *pmedium via CloneStgMedium().  ;  Protected *MatchedEntry.IDO_EntryStruct, *MyStgMedium.STGMEDIUM, *MyFormatEtc.FORMATETC  Protected RenderCB.ProtoIDORenderData, RenderUserData, EffectiveTymed, RetValue  Protected RenderedMed.STGMEDIUM, EntryFormatCopy.FORMATETC  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_" + Method$ + " ERROR: THIS IDATAOBJECT IS NOT VALID.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  If *pformatetcIn = #Null Or *pmedium = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_" + Method$ + " ERROR: *pformatetcIn or *pmedium is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ForEach *DataObjectDet\Entries()    *MyStgMedium = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_stgmed    *MyFormatEtc = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format    ; If delayed rendering has not run yet, rely on the advertised FORMATETC\tymed; otherwise use STGMEDIUM\tymed    If *DataObjectDet\Entries()\RenderCallback      EffectiveTymed = *MyFormatEtc\tymed    Else      EffectiveTymed = *MyStgMedium\tymed    EndIf    ;    ; Check cfFormat, dwAspect, and lindex (tolerating lindex = 0 when stored entry uses lindex = -1)    If *pformatetcIn\cfFormat = *MyFormatEtc\cfFormat      If *pformatetcIn\dwAspect = *MyFormatEtc\dwAspect Or *pformatetcIn\dwAspect = 0        If *pformatetcIn\lindex = *MyFormatEtc\lindex Or *pformatetcIn\lindex = -1 Or (*MyFormatEtc\lindex = -1 And *pformatetcIn\lindex = 0)          If (*pformatetcIn\tymed & EffectiveTymed) Or *pformatetcIn\tymed = 0 Or (EffectiveTymed = #TYMED_NULL And (*pformatetcIn\tymed & *MyFormatEtc\tymed))            ; Exact medium match found: prioritize it immediately and stop searching            *MatchedEntry = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()            Break          ElseIf *MatchedEntry = #Null            ; Fallback match: bidirectional synthesis between HGLOBAL/MFPICT and ISTREAM            If ((*pformatetcIn\tymed & #TYMED_ISTREAM) And (EffectiveTymed & (#TYMED_HGLOBAL | #TYMED_MFPICT))) Or ((*pformatetcIn\tymed & #TYMED_HGLOBAL) And (EffectiveTymed & #TYMED_ISTREAM))              *MatchedEntry = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()            EndIf          EndIf        EndIf      EndIf    EndIf  Next  ;  If *MatchedEntry = #Null    UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_" + Method$ + ": " + GetFormatName(*pformatetcIn\cfFormat) + "/" + GetTymedName(*pformatetcIn\tymed) + " ---> NOT FOUND")    ProcedureReturn #DV_E_FORMATETC  EndIf  ;  ; Extract delayed rendering callback info if this entry has not been materialized yet  RenderCB = *MatchedEntry\RenderCallback  If RenderCB    RenderUserData = *MatchedEntry\UserData    CopyMemory(@*MatchedEntry\m_format, @EntryFormatCopy, SizeOf(FormatEtc))  EndIf  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  ; Execute the delayed-rendering callback outside the mutex lock so callbacks can safely call IDataObject helpers  If RenderCB    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_" + Method$ + ": Triggering delayed rendering callback for " + GetFormatName(EntryFormatCopy\cfFormat))    RetValue = RenderCB(*DataObjectDet, @EntryFormatCopy, @RenderedMed, RenderUserData)    If RetValue <> #S_OK      IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_" + Method$ + ": Delayed rendering callback failed -> " + GetWinErrorMessage(RetValue))      ProcedureReturn RetValue    EndIf    ; Cache the materialized medium into the entry once and clear RenderCallback    LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    If *MatchedEntry\RenderCallback      CopyMemory(@RenderedMed, @*MatchedEntry\m_stgmed, SizeOf(StgMedium))      *MatchedEntry\RenderCallback = #Null    Else      ; Another thread materialized or replaced this entry in the meantime; discard our duplicate      ReleaseStgMedium_(@RenderedMed)    EndIf    UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  EndIf  ;  ; Duplicate the stored medium (or synthesize HGLOBAL <-> ISTREAM) into *pmedium  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  RetValue = CloneStgMedium(*DataObjectDet, @*MatchedEntry\m_stgmed, *pmedium, *pformatetcIn, Method$)  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  ProcedureReturn RetValueEndProcedure;;; *******************************************************************;;-                       Delayed Rendering;; *******************************************************************;Procedure RegisterDelayedData(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetc.FORMATETC, *RenderCallback, UserData = 0)  ;  ; Role: Registers a format for delayed (on-demand) rendering inside *DataObjectDet.  ;       The format is immediately advertised by EnumFormatEtc and QueryGetData, while the actual  ;       STGMEDIUM content is generated only upon the first GetData / GetDataHere call via *RenderCallback.  ; Parameters:  ;   *DataObjectDet  - Pointer to the owning IDataObject / IDO_DetailsStruct.  ;   *pformatetc     - FORMATETC describing the advertised format and tymed.  ;   *RenderCallback - Address of a ProtoIDORenderData procedure.  ;   UserData        - Optional custom integer passed back to *RenderCallback.  ; Output: Returns #S_OK on success, or a standard COM HRESULT error code.  ;  Protected *Entry.IDO_EntryStruct, *NewPtd, tdSize  Protected *AdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  ElseIf *pformatetc = #Null Or *RenderCallback = #Null Or *pformatetc\cfFormat = 0    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  ; Duplicate optional DVTARGETDEVICE structure (*pformatetc\ptd) if present  If *pformatetc\ptd And IsPTRValid(*pformatetc\ptd)    tdSize = PeekL(*pformatetc\ptd)    If tdSize >= SizeOf(LONG)      *NewPtd = CoTaskMemAlloc_(tdSize)      If *NewPtd        CopyMemory(*pformatetc\ptd, *NewPtd, tdSize)      Else        ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY      EndIf    EndIf  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ; Look for an existing entry matching cfFormat, dwAspect, lindex, and tymed to update in place  ForEach *DataObjectDet\Entries()    If *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\cfFormat = *pformatetc\cfFormat And *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\dwAspect = *pformatetc\dwAspect And *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\lindex = *pformatetc\lindex And *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\tymed = *pformatetc\tymed      *Entry = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()      Break    EndIf  Next  ;  If *Entry    ReleaseStgMedium_(@*Entry\m_stgmed)    ZeroMemory_(@*Entry\m_stgmed, SizeOf(StgMedium))    If *Entry\m_format\ptd      CoTaskMemFree_(*Entry\m_format\ptd)    EndIf  Else    If AddElement(*DataObjectDet\Entries()) = 0      UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)      If *NewPtd : CoTaskMemFree_(*NewPtd) : EndIf      ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY    EndIf    *Entry = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()  EndIf  ;  CopyMemory(*pformatetc, @*Entry\m_format, SizeOf(FormatEtc))  *Entry\m_format\ptd   = *NewPtd  *Entry\RenderCallback = *RenderCallback  *Entry\UserData       = UserData  *AdviseHolder         = *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  ; Notify advise sinks outside the mutex lock to avoid cross-thread deadlocks  If *AdviseHolder    *AdviseHolder\SendOnDataChange(*DataObjectDet, 0, 0)  EndIf  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("RegisterDelayedData: Registered delayed format " + GetFormatName(*pformatetc\cfFormat) + "/" + GetTymedName(*pformatetc\tymed))  ProcedureReturn #S_OKEndProcedure;; *******************************************************************;;-                 The twelve methods of the IDataObject;; *******************************************************************;; Although COM callers pass an 'IDataObject' pointer as the first parameter ('this'); to every method, our IDataObject pointers also point directly to the enclosing; 'IDO_DetailsStruct' structure (since pDataObject is at offset 0).;Procedure dataobject_GetData(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetcIn.FORMATETC, *pmedium.STGMEDIUM)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::GetData. Renders the data described in *pformatetcIn  ;       and transfers it through a newly allocated medium in *pmedium.  ;  ProcedureReturn IDO_GetDataInternal(*DataObjectDet, *pformatetcIn, *pmedium, "GetData")EndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_GetDataHere(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetcIn.FORMATETC, *pmedium.STGMEDIUM)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::GetDataHere. Renders the data described in *pformatetcIn  ;       directly into the caller-allocated medium (IStream or IStorage) supplied in *pmedium.  ;  ProcedureReturn IDO_GetDataInternal(*DataObjectDet, *pformatetcIn, *pmedium, "GetDataHere")EndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_EnumFormatEtc(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, dwDirection, *ppenumFormatEtc.Integer)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::EnumFormatEtc. Creates and returns an IEnumFORMATETC  ;       enumerator object via Windows' standard SHCreateStdEnumFmtEtc_() API.  ;  Protected tx$, *FormatEtcArray, EntryCount, i, RetValue  ;  If *ppenumFormatEtc = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumFormatEtc ERROR: *ppenumFormatEtc is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  *ppenumFormatEtc\i = #Null  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumFormatEtc ERROR: THIS IDATAOBJECT IS NOT VALID.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  ;  tx$ = "dataobject_EnumFormatEtc called with "  If dwDirection = #DATADIR_GET    tx$ + "#DATADIR_GET"  ElseIf dwDirection = #DATADIR_SET    tx$ + "#DATADIR_SET"  Else    tx$ + "invalid direction (" + Str(dwDirection) + ")"  EndIf  IDO_RegisterResults(tx$)  ;  If dwDirection = #DATADIR_GET    LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    EntryCount = ListSize(*DataObjectDet\Entries())    If EntryCount = 0      UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)      IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumFormatEtc error: No format in the object.")      ProcedureReturn #E_NOTIMPL    EndIf    ; Build a contiguous C-style array of FORMATETC structures from our Entries() list    *FormatEtcArray = AllocateMemory(SizeOf(FormatEtc) * EntryCount)    If *FormatEtcArray = #Null      UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)      ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY    EndIf    i = 0    ForEach *DataObjectDet\Entries()      CopyMemory(@*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format, *FormatEtcArray + (i * SizeOf(FormatEtc)), SizeOf(FormatEtc))      i + 1    Next    UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    ;    RetValue = SHCreateStdEnumFmtEtc_(EntryCount, *FormatEtcArray, *ppenumFormatEtc)    FreeMemory(*FormatEtcArray)    If RetValue = #S_OK      IDO_RegisterResults("   -> SHCreateStdEnumFmtEtc_ called successfully")    Else      IDO_RegisterResults("   -> SHCreateStdEnumFmtEtc_ error in dataobject_EnumFormatEtc: " + GetWinErrorMessage(RetValue))    EndIf    ProcedureReturn RetValue  ElseIf dwDirection = #DATADIR_SET    ProcedureReturn #E_NOTIMPL  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARGEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_SetData(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetc.FORMATETC, *pmedium.STGMEDIUM, fRelease)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::SetData. Stores or updates data inside the IDataObject for  ;       the specified *pformatetc and *pmedium. Supports TYMED_GDI (#CF_BITMAP and #CF_PALETTE),  ;       TYMED_HGLOBAL, TYMED_ENHMF, TYMED_MFPICT, TYMED_FILE, TYMED_ISTORAGE, TYMED_ISTREAM, and TYMED_NULL.  ;  Protected tx$, RetValue, tdSize  Protected *Entry.IDO_EntryStruct, *NewPtd  Protected *AdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder  Protected TempStgMed.STGMEDIUM  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_SetData ERROR: THIS IDATAOBJECT IS NOT VALID.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  If *pformatetc = #Null Or *pmedium = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_SetData ERROR: *pformatetc or *pmedium is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  tx$ = "dataobject_SetData received: " + GetFormatName(*pformatetc\cfFormat) + " - " + GetTymedName(*pmedium\tymed) + "."  If *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_NULL And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_GDI And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_HGLOBAL And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_ENHMF And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_MFPICT And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_FILE And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_ISTORAGE And *pmedium\tymed <> #TYMED_ISTREAM    tx$ + " / This Tymed is not implemented! (" + GetTymedName(*pmedium\tymed) + ")"    IDO_RegisterResults(tx$)    ProcedureReturn #E_NOTIMPL  EndIf  IDO_RegisterResults(tx$)  ;  ; Duplicate the incoming medium into TempStgMed first so existing data remains intact if cloning fails  RetValue = CloneStgMedium(*DataObjectDet, *pmedium, @TempStgMed, *pformatetc, "SetData")  If RetValue <> #S_OK    ProcedureReturn RetValue  EndIf  ;  ; Duplicate optional DVTARGETDEVICE structure (*pformatetc\ptd) if present so we never keep a dangling pointer  If *pformatetc\ptd And IsPTRValid(*pformatetc\ptd)    tdSize = PeekL(*pformatetc\ptd)    If tdSize >= SizeOf(LONG)      *NewPtd = CoTaskMemAlloc_(tdSize)      If *NewPtd        CopyMemory(*pformatetc\ptd, *NewPtd, tdSize)      Else        ReleaseStgMedium_(@TempStgMed)        ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY      EndIf    EndIf  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ; Search Entries() for an existing entry with identical cfFormat, dwAspect, lindex, and tymed  ForEach *DataObjectDet\Entries()    If *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\cfFormat = *pformatetc\cfFormat And *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\dwAspect = *pformatetc\dwAspect And *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\lindex = *pformatetc\lindex And *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\tymed = *pformatetc\tymed      *Entry = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()      Break    EndIf  Next  ;  If *Entry    ReleaseStgMedium_(@*Entry\m_stgmed)    If *Entry\m_format\ptd      CoTaskMemFree_(*Entry\m_format\ptd)    EndIf  Else    If AddElement(*DataObjectDet\Entries()) = 0      UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)      If *NewPtd : CoTaskMemFree_(*NewPtd) : EndIf      ReleaseStgMedium_(@TempStgMed)      ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY    EndIf    *Entry = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()  EndIf  ;  CopyMemory(*pformatetc, @*Entry\m_format, SizeOf(FormatEtc))  *Entry\m_format\ptd   = *NewPtd  CopyMemory(@TempStgMed, @*Entry\m_stgmed, SizeOf(StgMedium))  *Entry\RenderCallback = #Null  *Entry\UserData       = 0  *AdviseHolder         = *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  If fRelease    ; Release the caller's original medium upon successful ownership transfer    ReleaseStgMedium_(*pmedium)    IDO_RegisterResults("   SetData ---> ORIGINAL DATA HAS BEEN RELEASED")  EndIf  ;  ; Notify any registered DAdvise sinks outside the mutex lock  If *AdviseHolder    *AdviseHolder\SendOnDataChange(*DataObjectDet, 0, 0)  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn #S_OKEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_QueryInterface(*pDataObject.IDataObject, iid, *ppvObject.Integer)  ;  ; Role: Implements IUnknown::QueryInterface. Returns a pointer to the requested interface  ;       (IUnknown or IDataObject) in *ppvObject and increments the object's reference count.  ;  If *ppvObject = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryInterface ERROR: *ppvObject is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  *ppvObject\i = #Null  ;  If IsIDataObject(*pDataObject) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryInterface ERROR: Invalid *pDataObject -> " + Str(*pDataObject))    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  ElseIf iid = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryInterface ERROR: iid is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  If CompareMemory(iid, ?IID_IUnknown, 16) Or CompareMemory(iid, ?IID_IDataObject, 16)    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryInterface: OK")    *ppvObject\i = *pDataObject    *pDataObject\AddRef()    ProcedureReturn #S_OK  EndIf  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryInterface: #E_NOINTERFACE -> " + StringFromCLSID(iid))  ProcedureReturn #E_NOINTERFACEEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_AddRef(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct)  ;  ; Role: Implements IUnknown::AddRef. Increments the reference count in a thread-safe manner.  ; Output: Returns the updated reference count.  ;  Protected NewRefCount  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet)    LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    *DataObjectDet\Refcount + 1    NewRefCount = *DataObjectDet\Refcount    UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_AddRef: Refcount = " + Str(NewRefCount))    ProcedureReturn NewRefCount  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn 0EndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_Release(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct)  ;  ; Role: Implements IUnknown::Release. Decrements the reference count for this IDataObject instance  ;       and frees all owned media, target devices, advise holders, and tracking structures when it reaches 0.  ; Output: Returns the remaining reference count (0 when the object has been destroyed).  ;  Shared IDO_Details()  Protected RemainingRef, ct  Protected *AdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    ProcedureReturn 0  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  *DataObjectDet\Refcount - 1  RemainingRef = *DataObjectDet\Refcount  If RemainingRef > 0    UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_Release: Object is still in use: RefCount = " + Str(RemainingRef))    ProcedureReturn RemainingRef  EndIf  ; Detach the advise holder before unlocking so we can notify sinks safely without holding IDO_Mutex  *AdviseHolder = *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder  *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder = #Null  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_Release: Destroying object...")  If *AdviseHolder    *AdviseHolder\SendOnDataChange(*DataObjectDet, 0, 64) ; #ADVF_DATAONSTOP = 64    *AdviseHolder\Release()  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ct = ListSize(*DataObjectDet\Entries())  ForEach *DataObjectDet\Entries()    ReleaseStgMedium_(@*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_stgmed)    If *DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\ptd      CoTaskMemFree_(*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format\ptd)    EndIf  Next  ClearList(*DataObjectDet\Entries())  ;  ForEach IDO_Details()    If IDO_Details() = *DataObjectDet      DeleteElement(IDO_Details())      Break    EndIf  Next  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  IDO_RegisterResults(" •  --> " + Str(ct) + " data entry(ies) and the IDO_Details() element have been released.")  ProcedureReturn 0EndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_QueryGetData(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetcIn.FormatEtc)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::QueryGetData. Determines whether a subsequent call to GetData  ;       would succeed for the specified *pformatetcIn structure (including delayed and synthesized formats).  ; Output: Returns #S_OK if supported, or the specific #DV_E_* diagnostic code required by Windows OLE.  ;  Protected *MyFormatEtc.FORMATETC, *MyStgMedium.StgMedium  Protected FormatFound, AspectFound, LindexFound, EffectiveTymed  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData error: E_POINTER.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  ElseIf *pformatetcIn = #Null Or *pformatetcIn\cfFormat = 0    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData error: E_INVALIDARG.")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  ; Evaluate each registered format in hierarchical order: cfFormat -> dwAspect -> lindex -> tymed  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ForEach *DataObjectDet\Entries()    *MyStgMedium = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_stgmed    *MyFormatEtc = @*DataObjectDet\Entries()\m_format    If *DataObjectDet\Entries()\RenderCallback      EffectiveTymed = *MyFormatEtc\tymed    Else      EffectiveTymed = *MyStgMedium\tymed    EndIf    ;    If *pformatetcIn\cfFormat = *MyFormatEtc\cfFormat      FormatFound = #True      If *pformatetcIn\dwAspect = *MyFormatEtc\dwAspect Or *pformatetcIn\dwAspect = 0        AspectFound = #True        ; Accept -1 as a wildcard, and tolerate lindex = 0 when the stored entry uses lindex = -1        If *pformatetcIn\lindex = *MyFormatEtc\lindex Or *pformatetcIn\lindex = -1 Or (*MyFormatEtc\lindex = -1 And *pformatetcIn\lindex = 0)          LindexFound = #True          ; Check direct tymed match or bidirectional HGLOBAL/MFPICT <-> ISTREAM synthesis capability          If *pformatetcIn\tymed = 0 Or (*pformatetcIn\tymed & *MyFormatEtc\tymed) Or (*pformatetcIn\tymed & EffectiveTymed) Or ((*pformatetcIn\tymed & #TYMED_ISTREAM) And (EffectiveTymed & (#TYMED_HGLOBAL | #TYMED_MFPICT))) Or ((*pformatetcIn\tymed & #TYMED_HGLOBAL) And (EffectiveTymed & #TYMED_ISTREAM))            UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)            IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData with " + GetFormatName(*pformatetcIn\cfFormat) + "/" + GetTymedName(*pformatetcIn\tymed) + " --> OK/Found.")            ProcedureReturn #S_OK          EndIf        EndIf      EndIf    EndIf  Next  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  ; Return the exact OLE error code corresponding to the first mismatched attribute  If FormatFound = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData: " + GetFormatName(*pformatetcIn\cfFormat) + " --> NOT FOUND (#DV_E_FORMATETC)")    ProcedureReturn #DV_E_FORMATETC  ElseIf AspectFound = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData: DVASPECT #" + Str(*pformatetcIn\dwAspect) + " --> NOT FOUND (#DV_E_DVASPECT)")    ProcedureReturn #DV_E_DVASPECT  ElseIf LindexFound = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData: lindex #" + Str(*pformatetcIn\lindex) + " --> NOT FOUND (#DV_E_LINDEX)")    ProcedureReturn #DV_E_LINDEX  EndIf  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_QueryGetData: " + GetTymedName(*pformatetcIn\tymed) + "/" + GetFormatName(*pformatetcIn\cfFormat) + " --> NOT FOUND (#DV_E_TYMED)")  ProcedureReturn #DV_E_TYMEDEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetcIn.FormatEtc, *pformatetcOut.FormatEtc)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::GetCanonicalFormatEtc. Provides a canonical (device-independent)  ;       equivalent of *pformatetcIn in *pformatetcOut.  ;  Protected RetValue  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc error: E_POINTER.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  ElseIf *pformatetcIn = #Null Or *pformatetcOut = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc error: E_INVALIDARG.")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc with " + GetFormatName(*pformatetcIn\cfFormat))  ;  CopyMemory(*pformatetcIn, *pformatetcOut, SizeOf(FormatEtc))  *pformatetcOut\ptd = #Null  ;  RetValue = dataobject_QueryGetData(*DataObjectDet, *pformatetcIn)  If RetValue <> #S_OK    ZeroMemory_(*pformatetcOut, SizeOf(FormatEtc))    ProcedureReturn RetValue  EndIf  ;  ; Per Microsoft specification: if the input ptd was already NULL, we MUST return #DATA_S_SAMEFORMATETC  If *pformatetcIn\ptd = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc: Input ptd is NULL -> #DATA_S_SAMEFORMATETC.")    ProcedureReturn #DATA_S_SAMEFORMATETC  EndIf  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc: Stripped non-null ptd -> #S_OK.")  ProcedureReturn #S_OKEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_DAdvise(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *pformatetc.FORMATETC, advf, *padvSink.IAdviseSink, *pdwConnection.Long)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::DAdvise. Establishes an advisory notification connection between  ;       this IDataObject and the caller's *padvSink via Windows' standard CreateDataAdviseHolder_().  ;  Protected RetValue, *AdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder  ;  If *pdwConnection = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise error: *pdwConnection is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  *pdwConnection\l = 0  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise error: E_POINTER.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  ElseIf *padvSink = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise error: *padvSink is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_INVALIDARG  EndIf  ;  If *pformatetc And *pformatetc\cfFormat <> 0    If dataobject_QueryGetData(*DataObjectDet, *pformatetc) <> #S_OK      IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise error: Requested format (" + GetTymedName(*pformatetc\tymed) + "/" + GetFormatName(*pformatetc\cfFormat) + ") is not supported.")      ProcedureReturn #OLE_E_ADVISENOTSUPPORTED    EndIf  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  If *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder = #Null    CreateDataAdviseHolder_(@*DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder)  EndIf  *AdviseHolder = *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  If *AdviseHolder = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise error: Failed to create IDataAdviseHolder.")    ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY  EndIf  ;  RetValue = *AdviseHolder\Advise(*DataObjectDet, *pformatetc, advf, *padvSink, *pdwConnection)  If RetValue = #S_OK    If *pformatetc      IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise: Connection ID " + Str(*pdwConnection\l) + " registered for " + GetTymedName(*pformatetc\tymed) + "/" + GetFormatName(*pformatetc\cfFormat) + ".")    Else      IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise: Wildcard connection ID " + Str(*pdwConnection\l) + " registered.")    EndIf  Else    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DAdvise error: Unable to register advise sink: " + GetWinErrorMessage(RetValue) + ".")  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn RetValueEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_DUnAdvise(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, dwConnection.l)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::DUnadvise. Removes an existing advisory notification connection  ;       previously established through dataobject_DAdvise().  ;  Protected RetValue, *AdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DUnAdvise error: E_POINTER.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  *AdviseHolder = *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  If dwConnection = 0 Or *AdviseHolder = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DUnAdvise error: No active connection (#OLE_E_NOCONNECTION).")    ProcedureReturn #OLE_E_NOCONNECTION  EndIf  ;  RetValue = *AdviseHolder\Unadvise(dwConnection)  If RetValue = #S_OK    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DUnAdvise: Connection ID " + Str(dwConnection) + " successfully unregistered.")  Else    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_DUnAdvise error: Unable to unregister advise sink: " + GetWinErrorMessage(RetValue) + ".")  EndIf  ;  ProcedureReturn RetValueEndProcedure;Procedure dataobject_EnumDAdvise(*DataObjectDet.IDO_DetailsStruct, *ppenumAdvise.Integer)  ;  ; Role: Implements IDataObject::EnumDAdvise. Returns an IEnumSTATDATA enumerator listing  ;       all advisory connections currently registered on this IDataObject.  ;  Protected SC, *AdviseHolder.IDataAdviseHolder  ;  If *ppenumAdvise = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumDAdvise error: *ppenumAdvise is null.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  *ppenumAdvise\i = #Null  ;  If IsIDataObject(*DataObjectDet) = #False    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumDAdvise error: E_POINTER.")    ProcedureReturn #E_POINTER  EndIf  ;  LockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  If *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder = #Null    CreateDataAdviseHolder_(@*DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder)  EndIf  *AdviseHolder = *DataObjectDet\pDataAdviseHolder  UnlockMutex(IDO_Mutex)  ;  If *AdviseHolder = #Null    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumDAdvise error: Failed to create IDataAdviseHolder.")    ProcedureReturn #E_OUTOFMEMORY  EndIf  ;  SC = *AdviseHolder\EnumAdvise(*ppenumAdvise)  If SC <> #S_OK    IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumDAdvise error: EnumAdvise failed: " + GetWinErrorMessage(SC) + ".")    ProcedureReturn SC  EndIf  ;  IDO_RegisterResults("dataobject_EnumDAdvise: Successfully created IEnumSTATDATA.")  ProcedureReturn #S_OKEndProcedure;DataSection  VTable_IDataObject:    Data.i @dataobject_QueryInterface(), @dataobject_AddRef(), @dataobject_Release()    Data.i @dataobject_GetData(), @dataobject_GetDataHere(), @dataobject_QueryGetData()    Data.i @dataobject_GetCanonicalFormatEtc(), @dataobject_SetData(), @dataobject_EnumFormatEtc()    Data.i @dataobject_DAdvise(), @dataobject_DUnAdvise(), @dataobject_EnumDAdvise()    ;  IID_IOleObject:   ; "{00000112-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}"    Data.l $00000112    Data.w $0000, $0000    Data.b $C0, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $46    ;  CLSID_DataObject: ; "{00000320-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}"    Data.l $00000320    Data.w $0000, $0000    Data.b $C0, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $46    ;  IID_IDataObject:  ; "{0000010E-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}"    Data.l $0000010E    Data.w $0000, $0000    Data.b $C0, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $46    ;  IID_IUnknown:     ; "{00000000-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}"    Data.l $00000000    Data.w $0000, $0000    Data.b $C0, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $46    ;  IID_IStream:      ; "{0000000C-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}"    Data.l $0000000C    Data.w $0000, $0000    Data.b $C0, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $46    ;  IID_IStorage:     ; "{0000000B-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}"    Data.l $0000000B    Data.w $0000, $0000    Data.b $C0, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $46  EndDataSection  ;; IDE Options = PureBasic 6.41 (Windows - x64); CursorPosition = 844; FirstLine = 441; Folding = -XEA9; EnableXP; DPIAware